<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ludovico III Gonzaga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1412–1478</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Ludovico III, Marquis of Mantua</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ludovico III Gonzaga (1412–1478) was Marquis of Mantua from 1444 and a condottiere in the service of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>. A patron of humanism and the arts, he employed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrea-mantegna">Andrea Mantegna</a> as court painter and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leon-battista-alberti">Leon Battista Alberti</a>, who designed the churches of Sant'Andrea and San Sebastiano in Mantua. Mantegna's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camera-degli-sposi">Camera degli Sposi</a> portrays him with his family and court.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ludovico-iii-gonzaga.jpg" alt="Ludovico III Gonzaga" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrea Mantegna · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andrea_Mantegna_057.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
